    "result_text": "All tests pass (3/3, BUILD SUCCESS) and there's only the one acceptance test class in the repo.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the optional owner `postcode` with region-based validation, keeping structural impact low by isolating new behaviour in small, cohesive units and avoiding edits to the large `ExceptionControllerAdvice` and `OwnerMapper` classes.\n\n**Changes (5 files):**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `postcode` property (not in `required`) to the `OwnerFields` schema with `pattern: '^\\d{4}$'`. This regenerates the request/response DTOs with the field and, via the existing Bean Validation \u2192 `MethodArgumentNotValidException` \u2192 400 path, rejects a malformed postcode automatically (no Java needed).\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a `postcode` field with `@Column` plus a plain getter/setter, so it's persisted and returned. MapStruct auto-maps it in both directions, so **`OwnerMapper` needed no change**.\n\n3. **`db/hsqldb/schema.sql`** \u2014 Added `postcode VARCHAR(4)` to the `owners` table. Only the hsqldb schema (used by tests, `ddl-auto=none`) tracks the full column set; h2/postgres/mysql rely on `ddl-auto=update`, matching how prior columns (`registration_date`, `customer_code`, `namesake_count`) were handled.\n\n4. **`Postcode.java`** (new) \u2014 A tiny single-method util that reuses the existing `Locality` city\u2192region table and checks the NSW/VIC/QLD ranges. Returns `true` for absent postcodes and unknown-region cities (permissive default). WMC_other \u2248 0.\n\n5. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 One import plus a 3-line guard that returns `400 BAD_REQUEST` when a supplied postcode is out of range for the city's region.\n\nThe request contract stays backward-compatible: owners created without a postcode are still accepted. Malformed postcodes (e.g. `\"12\"`) get 400 from the schema pattern; out-of-range-for-region postcodes get 400 from the guard.",
